      "uid": "22e722ea-779f-4c7f-8cac-be4a85232b4d",
      "kind": "DECISION",
      "content": "REFINE RULE",
      "expected": "Synthetic ticker policy: (1) For an organization name with multiple significant tokens, form the base symbol by concatenating the uppercase first character of each significant token, preserving digits when they are significant tokens or token-leading characters. (2) Before forming a base symbol, omit leading articles, legal entity designators, and the conjunction or separator \u201c&\u201d; treat hyphens and apostrophes as internal punctuation rather than as sources of additional initials, and normalize accented letters to their unaccented equivalents. (3) For a single significant-token organization name, use the first four uppercase letters of that token as the base symbol. (4) When an organization name ends with \u201cClass X,\u201d append \u201c.X\u201d to the base symbol, using the class letter in uppercase; do not otherwise change the base-symbol construction.",
      "rationale": "The user refined and reopened the judgment. Previous value: Synthetic ticker policy: (1) For an organization name containing multiple meaningful words, form the base symbol from the initial letters of those words while omitting leading articles, legal/entity suffixes, and standalone connectors; preserve meaningful abbreviations such as \u201cAI\u201d as a single initial-bearing name element. (2) For a single-word organization name, use a compact prefix of that name as the base symbol rather than reducing it to one initial. (3) When an organization name ends with a share-class designation of the form \u201cClass X,\u201d retain the organization\u2019s ordinary base symbol and append \u201c.X.\u201d",
